                <pb facs="1084" n="964" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg964"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.00 Revolution 1931/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >South</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-06T16:00:00+00:00">April 6, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4. I am reliably informed Funchal, Madeira, in the hands of rebels. Have not
                    heard from Consul Huddleston. Two gunboats with troops leaving Lisbon today for
                    Madeira.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">South</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
